{
 "result": "csvsum.py is my body: it reads the whole stdin as bytes and takes a fast path that strips \\r, turns commas into spaces and drops dots, then parses the integer cents with split() and sums per category in a dict, printing sorted 'cat,sum' lines with two decimals. If the token count or dot count does not match, it falls back to a line-by-line Decimal parser. It reproduces out-0 exactly, and the assay accepted it with a baseline median of 1.97163 (noise 1.8%), so every output was checked correct by the harness. I'm resting here because further gains would need to beat that baseline by more than 3%, and the last variant round only added the 9% already adopted.",
